  "question": {
    "text": "A fully charged capacitor&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math> with initial charge <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math> is connected to an ideal inductor of self-inductance&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi></math> at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>. The time at which energy is stored equally between the electric and the magnetic fields is"
  },
